id: aflame
name: Aflame
kind: battlefield
envQuality: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Burning ground. 2(bT) Life Points at the start and end of your turn, and 1(bT) more
  for every stack of Broken you are carrying.
text: >
  Aflame: If you start or end your Turn in this Battle Environment, reduce your Life
  Points by 2(bT). Increase this reduction by 1(bT) for every stack of the Broken Combat
  Condition you're suffering from.

---

# "If you start or end your Turn" - both, so this is two blocks and not one. They are the
# same rule written twice rather than one block on two Moments, because a block belongs to
# one Moment and saying it twice is honest about how often it fires: standing in fire for a
# full turn costs you twice.
#
# --- The Broken it feeds on ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Increase this reduction by 1(bT) for every stack of the Broken Combat Condition you're
# suffering from."
#
# Read off the character rather than counted here, so a stack arriving from anywhere counts
# - the Lava and Magma Environments hand them out, and being Aflame in the lava is the
# obvious way to find out what that is worth.
#
# Life Points reduced rather than Damage: nothing Soaks this, which is the wording
# Poisoned, Suffocating and Collision Damage all use.

[automatic/start-of-turn]
life.value -= 2(bT) + 1(bT) * conditions.broken;

[automatic/end-of-turn]
life.value -= 2(bT) + 1(bT) * conditions.broken;
